<!--
  F5 — FCM small notification icon.

  Android renders the notification small-icon as a MONOCHROME MASK: only the
  alpha channel is used and the shape is re-tinted by the system (the app's
  accent on most launchers). A colored/opaque asset therefore shows up as a
  solid WHITE SQUARE. So this is a WHITE silhouette on a TRANSPARENT background
  (android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF" over no background) — a simple bell, the
  universal notification mark.

  This ships a VALID silhouette so the icon never renders as a white blob. A
  brand-accurate BuildSmart mark (the hard-hat / "BS" glyph as a clean
  single-color silhouette) is a FOLLOW-UP design asset — drop it in here at the
  same name and the wiring is unchanged.
-->
